# guardian_gold_futures_mgc_v0_2_prototype.pine provenance:
#   60484f4f… — 2026-08-11 F4 EOD force-flat added (operator-directed after
#               v0.1's sizing-fix re-run confirmed correct: median loser
#               -0.344% vs 0.34% target, N-ACT re-derived at 45.4% zero-trade
#               weeks). All four FRIENDLY firms auto-liquidate open positions
#               daily at the platform level — mandatory, not a rule choice —
#               so v0.1's inherited maxHoldBars=850 multi-day hold could never
#               execute as backtested at any of them. Closes any open
#               position at an explicit America/New_York flat time (default
#               16:45 ET, Tradeify's published deadline), independent of the
#               chart's display timezone or CME's own Chicago exchange
#               default. No entry-signal change — re-entry next session still
#               depends entirely on the untouched locked recoveryLong signal.
#               Supersedes v0_1 for decision-grade use; v0_1 retained as the
#               sizing-fix-only record. pine_check.py clean 2026-08-11.
#               Flagged, not fixed: the locked file's OWN session/hour/day
#               gates use bare hour/dayofweek (chart-timezone-dependent, not
#               code-guaranteed UTC) — unverified on MGC1!, see file header.
