# guardian_gold_futures_mgc_v0_3_prototype.pine provenance:
#   0f0aa817… — 2026-08-11 F5 fix (operator-directed after v0.2's re-run showed
#               all 199 EOD-flat exits filling at exactly 18:00, not ~16:45).
#               Root cause CONFIRMED by web search (not assumed): CME Globex
#               halts electronic trading 17:00-18:00 ET Mon-Thu for daily
#               maintenance. v0.2's F4 signal fired correctly on the 16:45 ET
#               bar (still open, pre-halt), but strategy.close() with
#               process_orders_on_close=false fills at the next bar's open —
#               and since 17:00-18:00 has no bars, that next bar is the 18:00
#               reopen. Same defect class + fix shape as the Aegis->6J port's
#               own F1 (EOD cutoff firing on a post-maintenance bar). FIX:
#               flatMinuteET default 45 -> 15 — signal now fires at 16:15 ET,
#               fill lands at the 16:30 ET bar open, a 15-min/1-bar buffer
#               before both the true 16:45 ET target and the 17:00 ET halt.
#               Also adds a dashboard row showing syminfo.timezone directly,
#               to settle (rather than infer from entry-hour clustering)
#               whether this COMEX symbol's bare hour/dayofweek resolve in
#               UTC as the locked file's comments claim. Supersedes v0_2 for
#               decision-grade use. pine_check.py clean 2026-08-11.
0f0aa81712baacd5080092c009b937c0416b029ce181ab53ddd194980871c56d  core/strategies/_archive/guardian/guardian_gold_futures_mgc_v0_3_prototype.pine

